## What ReachAgent is

A Python (`uv`-managed, `>=3.13`) authorization-and-vulnerability testing agent for web/API targets. One FastAPI + vanilla-JS GUI is the *only* entry point (`uv run reachagent-gui`, no CLI/TUI). It builds a NetworkX **reachability graph** of a target (hosts, services, endpoints, parameters, identities, sessions, findings), drives real HTTP/browser/proxy traffic through a role-bounded MCP tool surface, and confirms vulnerabilities via **LLM judgment** (`oracles/llm_judgment.py::judge()`) — not a deterministic decision table. A recently-shipped "v4 full-autonomy rebuild" removed the old confirmed/suspected two-tier findings split, removed manual confirmation gates, added a real Docker command-execution sandbox, and added dynamic multi-agent re-hunt spawning plus a GUI lane view to watch it happen live.

