**The `GET /api/scan/{id}/agents` endpoint** (v4 R3c) deserves its own note: it's a **pure read-side aggregation**, no new tracking state. It groups the existing `ScanEvent` stream by a `[label]` text prefix or `details["label"]` key that concurrent specialists/re-hunt agents already tag their own events with, and infers running/done status from a 20-second recency heuristic — *overridden* by the scan's own terminal lifecycle so a lane never reads "running" forever after the whole scan ends (a real bug an adversarial review caught and fixed).

