### Recon — `recon/`

**Purpose**: discovers the target's structure before/during exploitation. `recon/tools/` holds ~30 individual `ReconToolRunner` subclasses (nmap, masscan, ffuf, gobuster, nuclei, sqlmap, subfinder, ...) sharing one contract in `recon/tools/base.py`: `REACHAGENT_RECON_LIVE` env-gate → scope-enforce → binary-exists check → memory-guard → bounded `subprocess.run` (never `shell=True`) → parse into `Host`/`Service`/`Endpoint` facts only (never a `Finding`, never `write_finding`). Six of these (`nuclei`, `sqlmap`, `commix`, `dalfox`, `nikto`, `jwt_tool`) are instead `SignalGatedToolRunner`s (`recon/tools/signal_gated.py`) — they only fire when a prior graph fact already signals their vuln class, and their claims must be independently `run_oracle`-reconfirmed before ever becoming a finding; `REACHAGENT_AGGRESSIVE` is the one deliberate bypass of that signal-required gate (a target-intensity dial, not a confirmation-authority change).

