## Conventions

- **`uv run` everywhere, never bare `python`/`pip`.** GUI: `uv run reachagent-gui --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000`. Lint: `uv run ruff check --fix .` / format: `uv run ruff format .` / security lint: `uv run ruff check --select S .`. Type check: `uv run ty` (`uv run mypy` fallback — `pyproject.toml` actually configures `mypy strict=true`). Test: `uv run pytest`.
- **Ruff config**: `line-length=100`, `target-version=py313`, select `["E","F","I","W","UP","B","S"]`, excludes `third_party`/`.claude`/`.venv`. `tests/**` ignores `S101/S311/S105/S106`; `gui/**` ignores `E501` (long HTML/CSS/JS lines).
- **Test suite structure**: `tests/phase1` through `tests/phase12` are historical *build-order* milestones (stated directly in each dir's own module docstrings, e.g. `"""Phase 5 Coordinator scoring..."""`), not obviously named — inferred mapping: phase1=foundational execution/identity/recon+VAmPI gate, phase2=BOLA/IDOR chaining+crAPI gate, phase3=the big ~30-vuln-class driver buildout+Juice Shop gate, phase4=GraphQL, phase5=Coordinator, phase6=race+oracle-hardening, phase7=stateful exploration, phase8=signal-gated adapters, phase9=transport/evidence boundaries, phase10=durable resume, phase11=GUI, phase12=reporting/redaction. Non-numbered dirs (`scan/`, `recon/`, `graph/`, `gui/`, `sandbox/`, `report/`, `whitebox/`, `confirmation/`, etc.) are named by subsystem, added later.
- **Hermetic-test conventions**: real `httpx.MockTransport` wrapped in a real `httpx.Client` (the network boundary is faked, firer/client code runs for real) — never mocking the client itself. A shared `tests/_oracle_test_support.py` centralizes the fake-oracle-judgment client (`FixedJudgmentClient`, `fixed_oracle_runner`) and status constants (`CONFIRMS`/`DENIES`/`ALLOWS`/`INCONCLUSIVE`). Every LLM-advisory surface (guardian, confidence, recon tuning) has its own tests asserting the **fail-open** contract explicitly (no provider / malformed reply / exception → safe default, never propagates).
- **Live/eval tests**: gated `@pytest.mark.skipif(not _reachable(...), reason="needs X at Y")` — the reason string is always a self-contained "how to unskip this" instruction, not just "skipped".
- **Test naming**: long, sentence-like names encoding *why* the test exists (`test_dispatch_classes_one_driver_crashing_never_aborts_the_rest`, with a docstring citing the exact live incident that caused it), not just what it checks.
- **No reference-project names in the codebase** — patterns from external agentic-pentest tools are described generically in comments/docstrings ("a reference agent's own..."), never by name, per a standing project convention.
- **Docker eval targets, on-demand only**: bring up (`docker compose up -d`) only for a task that needs a live run; tear down (`docker compose down`) the moment it's done. VAmPI = `docker-compose.yml` (2 instances, :5000/:5002, toggle-only difference); crAPI = `docker-compose.crapi.yml` + external `CRAPI_COMPOSE_PATH` env var pointing at a separate local checkout (~10 containers); Juice Shop = `docker-compose.juiceshop.yml`; DVWA = `docker-compose.dvwa.yml` (needs a one-time manual `/setup.php` step).

## Gotchas

- **`.env` is never auto-loaded — zero `python-dotenv` usage anywhere in the codebase.** A bare `uv run pytest`/script shell has NO LLM provider even if `.env` has real credentials; every oracle call silently degrades to `inconclusive:no_llm_provider_configured` (0% recall in well under a second — looks like a detection bug, isn't one). Fix for a manual run: `set -a; source .env; set +a` before invoking. The GUI's own `/api/scan` path resolves a *saved* `config/providers.json` entry into per-scan env overrides instead, so it doesn't hit this.
- **Five GUI recon-tuning checkboxes are now dead no-ops.** `gui/app.py`'s `tuning_overrides` still sets `REACHAGENT_SURFACE_TUNING`/`REACHAGENT_SIGNAL_TUNING`/`REACHAGENT_TRANSPORT_TUNING`/`REACHAGENT_RECON_DEPTH_TUNING`/`REACHAGENT_WORDLIST_DEPTH_TUNING` from Settings-panel checkboxes, but a recent rebuild (`commit bbafce9`) removed the corresponding `flag_enabled(...)` checks from every one of the underlying recon modules — they now run unconditionally whenever a provider is configured, checkbox or not. Toggling these checkboxes currently changes nothing. `llm/runtime.py::override()` still auto-activates the same 5 (+`REACHAGENT_GUARDIAN_ADVISOR`) vestigial flag names, and `scan/entrypoint.py`'s docstrings for the depth/wordlist escalation functions still say "flag-gated, off by default" — also stale. **Not yet fixed** — a real, disclosed cleanup opportunity (delete the dead checkboxes/env-plumbing, or restore the flags if the intent was ever to make them optional again).
- **`config/providers.json` holds real-shaped API keys in plaintext** — verified correctly gitignored (`.gitignore:20`) and untracked, so not a repo-exposure risk, but worth remembering it's a live-credentials file on disk.
- **`SuspectedFinding` is fully gone** — if you see a reference to it in an old doc/plan/comment, that's stale; the current model is single-tier (`CONFIRMED_VIOLATION` or nothing), enforced at the `graph/store.py::add_finding` level independently of whatever called it.
- **Two named things are easy to confuse**: `sandbox/agent_shell.py` (real Docker shell, needs iptables+timeouts) vs. `sandbox/derive_value.py` (pure in-process expression evaluator, needs neither — its grammar can't express a loop). Also `oracles/registry.py::get_oracle()` (mechanism-name validation only) vs. `detection/oracle_gateway.py::registry_runner` (the actual live decision path via `judge()`) — don't assume the registry is where confirmation logic lives.
- **The Sandbox GUI tab deliberately does not use xterm.js** — a documented, disclosed simplification (a static append-only scrollback of already-captured text has no live PTY, so a terminal-emulator library buys nothing over a styled `<pre>` block).

## Navigation Guide

- **Add a new vulnerability class**: create a package under `src/reachagent/<vuln_class>/` following the common `Probe`/`Prober`/`Result`/`detect_*` shape (see "~29 vuln-class detectors" above for the template); wire it into `scan/orchestrator.py`'s dispatch list; add it to the `_CVSS_VECTOR`/`_WSTG`/`_CWE`/`_DESCRIPTION` tables in `report/professional.py`; add a `tests/phase3/test_<vuln_class>.py`.
- **Add a new recon tool**: subclass `recon/tools/base.py::ReconToolRunner` (fact-only) or `recon/tools/signal_gated.py::SignalGatedToolRunner` (claim-only, needs a `has_signal` graph-fact gate); register it in the relevant tool-family list in `scan/entrypoint.py`.
- **Change anything about scope enforcement**: `execution/scope.py::ScopeGuard` — remember `allowed_hosts()` also backs the sandbox's own egress firewall, so a change there has two consumers.
- **Change GUI live-state surfacing**: new state goes into `_scans[scan_id]` in `gui/app.py`; a new tab needs an `app.js` poll function + `index.html` tab entry + (usually) a new read-only GET route projecting off the shared `graph`/`audit`/`events` objects, never a new write path.
- **Investigate a confirmation/finding question**: start at `oracles/llm_judgment.py::judge()` (the actual decision), then `tools/validator.py::write_finding` (the only writer), then `graph/store.py::add_finding` (the last-line status guard).
- **Investigate a live-eval-gate question**: `eval/consolidated.py` for the composite runner, then the specific gate file (`harness.py` for VAmPI, `juiceshop_live.py`+`juiceshop_harness.py` for Juice Shop) — `eval/mcp_session.py` is the shared plumbing all of them build sessions from.
- **Run tests for one area**: `uv run pytest tests/<phase-or-subsystem-dir>/ -v` — see Conventions above for what each `phaseN` dir actually covers.
